    {
      "id": "claim_4381d8e279e94e45be0bc9370b79b373",
      "statement": "The repository is a pnpm TypeScript monorepo whose major domains are packages/shared (shared protocol and browser-agnostic logic), servers/mcp (agent-facing MCP surface), servers/websocket (the relay), and clients/extensions/{chrome,safari,firefox} (browser-side bridge packages), each with a distinct ownership boundary documented in AGENTS.md.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L111-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5491ed1ad7775e76d826adced2d8c8cdc32e175446768eb8f6c95307a33acd3d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0ecb9c713e4c4b3fa7a44ce9485cb90a",
      "statement": "The runtime path is a single explicit request/response chain with no continuous streaming: the user manually starts the bridge, the extension authenticates to the WebSocket relay with a pairing token and announces presence, the MCP server (also a relay client authenticated with the same token) forwards agent tool calls to the relay, and the relay delivers the request to the connected extension which reads or acts on the target tab and returns a structured result.",
      "evidence": [
